@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.6.1
@changelog
  - Codename: My whole brain is crying!
  - Automation: the UF1 follows automation. Its motor fader, the dB and pan readouts and the four volumes of the DAW view show what REAPER plays, envelope included.
  - Automation: the UF1 fader records in Touch. REAPER is told the fader is held for as long as the hand is on it, as it always was for the UF8.
  - Automation: faders let go when the hand does. Pan under FLIP (UF8 and UF1) records and returns on release, and a fader on a plug-in parameter ends its edit on release so Touch returns it like track volume: Plug-in Mode, SSL Strip Mode, FLIP onto a focused parameter and a Sticky Pot under FLIP. This was a known issue in v0.6.0.
  - Automation: a fader reports as touched only what it writes, so a fader on a plug-in parameter no longer makes REAPER write volume or pan points.
  - Automation: pots write a point. In Touch, with the transport running, each turn writes one point into the envelope at the play position, and the value stays until the envelope's next point, like a plug-in parameter on a pot. Track pan, track volume on a pot, send pan and send volume, on the UF8 and the UF1. One undo step per movement.
  - Automation: volume on a pot under FLIP no longer zigzags towards zero while automation plays, and the pan value on the UF8's display follows automation like its ring.
  - UF1: comes back up after being switched off and on; the unit ignores the first contact after power-on, and Rea-Sixty now opens it a second time.
  - UF1 and UF8: no fader sweep on connect.
  - UF1: an empty project blanks only the channel zone; soft-key names, bank header, time field and key lamps stay.
  - UF1: Items can take the fader. Settings, Bindings, UF1, JOG WHEEL, tick Fader = Item Volume on the Items row: the fader sets the volume of every selected item, the others by the same number of dB as the first.
  - UF1: the meter view's soft-key names come back after the MODE menu closes.
  - UF1: a Sticky Pot factory bank with Pin Sticky, Pair Sticky and Sticky OnOff.
  - Fixed: a crash when the UF1 was reopened while its display stream was running.
  - Meter view: the receiver for the SSL plug-ins' own data starts with REAPER, so goniometer, RTA and Loudness on the UF1 and the gate GR on the UC1 and the UF8's second GR row work without a script line. SSL 360 has to be closed while Rea-Sixty runs, as before.
  - Sticky Pot: a pin follows a CS or BC switch to the same control on the new plug-in, both targets of a paired pin. In Copy mode (A/B) it stays on the original.
  - FX Learn and the Learn HUD: the search field stays in view while the parameter list scrolls.
  - Settings, Bindings reopens on the surface tab you used last.
